## 7. A release tag deploys too, and the previous release stays for rollback
   concept: gitlab-ci-local --needs deploy runs deploy and what it depends on (build, which has no needs:, so every earlier stage); rolling back is pointing current at the previous release
   deploy > smoke ok
   deploy > deployed v1.4.0 to .deploy/current
    PASS  lint
    PASS  typecheck
    PASS  unit   100% coverage
    PASS  a11y
    PASS  audit
    PASS  build
    PASS  deploy
   pipeline finished in 56 s
   current -> releases/v1.4.0, release.json {"release":"v1.4.0","commit":"907db30f513e7fb0e7b98098a6169878e34c5421","source":"push"}; previous releases/scheduled-907db30f-1002 still on disk: true

## 8. The same pipeline on GitHub Actions and Azure Pipelines
   concept: github-actions/ci.yml and azure-pipelines.yml (neither runs here) have the same jobs, commands in the same order (coverage flag included), runners, deploy triggers and audit rule. GitHub: stages become needs, rules become if and on:. Azure: stages stay stages (each after the previous one), rules become conditions, runner tags become an environment's VM resource
   job        gitlab stage  github needs  azure stage (after)  runner      commands
   lint       lint                        lint                 any         npm run lint
   typecheck  typecheck     lint          typecheck (lint)     any         npm run typecheck
   unit       test          typecheck     test (typecheck)     any         npx vitest run --coverage
   a11y       test          typecheck     test (typecheck)     any         npm run a11y
   audit      audit         unit, a11y    audit (test)         any         npm run audit
   build      build         audit         build (audit)        any         npm run build
   deploy     deploy        build         deploy (build)       production  mkdir, cp dist, package.json, release.json, smoke releases/$RELEASE, ln -sfn, mv -T
   deploys on: schedule yes; push main no; tag v1.4.0 yes; tag v1.4.0-rc1 no; tag v1.4 no; tag rc-1 no
   audit blocks on: schedule yes; push main no; tag v1.4.0 yes
   the comparison on drifted copies. GitHub: smoke test after the switch, release.json dropped, deploy on ubuntu-latest, a loose tag filter and tag check:
   job        gitlab stage  github needs  azure stage (after)  runner      commands
   deploy     deploy        build         deploy (build)       gitlab production, github any, azure production DIFFERENT: gitlab mkdir, cp dist, package.json, release.json, smoke releases/$RELEASE, ln -sfn, mv -T | github mkdir, cp dist, package.json, ln -sfn, mv -T, smoke current | azure mkdir, cp dist, package.json, release.json, smoke releases/$RELEASE, ln -sfn, mv -T
   deploys on: schedule yes; push main no; tag v1.4.0 yes; tag v1.4.0-rc1 DIFFERENT (gitlab no, github yes, azure no); tag v1.4 no; tag rc-1 no
   audit blocks on: schedule yes; push main no; tag v1.4.0 yes
   Azure: the coverage flag dropped, the audit always only warns, the tag check step removed, deploy on a hosted agent:
   job        gitlab stage  github needs  azure stage (after)  runner      commands
   unit       test          typecheck     test (typecheck)     any         DIFFERENT: gitlab npx vitest run --coverage | github npx vitest run --coverage | azure npx vitest run
   deploy     deploy        build         deploy (build)       gitlab production, github production, azure any mkdir, cp dist, package.json, release.json, smoke releases/$RELEASE, ln -sfn, mv -T
   deploys on: schedule yes; push main no; tag v1.4.0 yes; tag v1.4.0-rc1 DIFFERENT (gitlab no, github no, azure yes); tag v1.4 DIFFERENT (gitlab no, github no, azure yes); tag rc-1 no
   audit blocks on: schedule DIFFERENT (gitlab yes, github yes, azure no); push main no; tag v1.4.0 DIFFERENT (gitlab yes, github yes, azure no)

